---
title: "Reactive inputs"
---

`{{< input >}}` emits a labeled control whose value is a reactive node. A `{js}` cell that
lists the name in `//| input:` re-runs when the control changes, including transitively.

Every control's value is also captured in the page URL, so a link restores the exact view
(and its downstream cells): change a control and copy the address to share that state.

{{< input name="k" type="slider" min="1" max="10" step="1" value="3" label="k" >}}

```{js}
//| name: doubled
//| input: k
return tali.value("k") * 2;
```

```{js}
//| input: doubled
const p = document.createElement("p");
p.textContent = "k doubled (transitively) = " + tali.get("doubled");
return p;
```

A number, a checkbox, a text box, and a dropdown, each driving their own cell:

{{< input name="n" type="number" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="20" label="n" >}}

```{js}
//| input: n
const p = document.createElement("p");
p.textContent = "n = " + tali.value("n");
return p;
```

{{< input name="on" type="checkbox" value="true" label="enabled" >}}

```{js}
//| input: on
const p = document.createElement("p");
p.textContent = tali.value("on") ? "enabled" : "disabled";
return p;
```

{{< input name="q" type="text" value="hello" label="query" >}}

```{js}
//| input: q
const p = document.createElement("p");
p.textContent = "query: " + tali.value("q");
return p;
```

{{< input name="c" type="select" options="alpha,beta,gamma" value="beta" label="channel" >}}

```{js}
//| input: c
const p = document.createElement("p");
p.textContent = "channel: " + tali.value("c");
return p;
```

One cell reading several inputs at once:

```{js}
//| input: k, n, on
const p = document.createElement("p");
p.textContent = `k=${tali.value("k")} n=${tali.value("n")} on=${tali.value("on")}`;
return p;
```

## `range` is `slider` under another name

`type="range"` is an accepted alias for `type="slider"`, so a document carried over from
a tool that spells it the HTML way keeps working instead of drawing an unknown-type
warning. Both spellings dispatch to the same control, which is what this pins: the one
below is indistinguishable from `k` above.

{{< input name="r" type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.1" value="0.4" label="r (range)" >}}

```{js}
//| input: r
const p = document.createElement("p");
p.textContent = "r = " + tali.value("r");
return p;
```
